estion/math-academy-id "q-20363" :question/problem "What would be the system of equations for the following augmented matrix?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$, $y$, and $z,$ then, the corresponding system of equations is \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0x+2y+3z=0 \\\\ 2x+0y+3z=2 \\\\ 2x+3y+0z=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy simplifying, we obtain: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2y+3z=0 \\\\ 2x+3z=2 \\\\ 2x+3y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-20363/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7c8f4da-c782-51e0-ac51-87a89f31860d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20363"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-20362/selection/d142f2b41ad610600d6818b84e2d6c725b74f96feec2590dc011733fd82d0b1f" :answer/id #uuid "594ce130-19c0-5d06-a4b3-29543169dcca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}2x+y+2z=1 \\\\ 3x+y+3z=-2 \\\\ x+3y+4z=3\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20362/selection/9227bd2c0424b24e2bc568dc0902701ab805ab6993e0205c606234246796267e" :answer/id #uuid "5aeef8a8-a92e-5354-8433-646beba43686" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}2x+y+2z=1 \\\\ 3x-2y+3z=2 \\\\ 4x+3y+4z=3\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20362/selection/b4d7548fe39ce68e897e85c4396596da725160fcdd231bc3494a5f9065804e27" :answer/id #uuid "1621e459-3620-5800-bc3a-5c40754f3810" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}2x+y+2z=1 \\\\ x+2y+3z=2 \\\\ 4x+3y+z=3\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20362/